1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:01,920
那是1956年。
It's 1956.

2
00:00:02,414 --> 00:00:11,360
一名年轻的程序员正带着他的女朋友在阿姆斯特丹逛街，他并不知道自己即将开发出
A young programmer is taking his girlfriend shopping in Amsterdam without knowing that he would develop one of the most important

3
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:13,636
历史上最重要的算法之一。
algorithms in history.

4
00:00:14,158 --> 00:00:21,668
没人能预料到，仅仅在20分钟内，我们所熟知的世界就会发生巨变。
No one could possibly know that in just 20 minutes the world as we knew it would be transformed.

5
00:00:22,158 --> 00:00:29,040
那是后来成为享誉世界的荷兰程序员和数学家 Edsger W.
That was the day when a soon-to-be a world-renowned Dutch programmer and mathematician, Etsker W.

6
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:37,220
Dijkstra，构思出一个将驱动GPS导航、网络路由、社交网络、
Dijkstra, came up with an algorithm that would power GPS navigation, network routing, social media networks,

7
00:00:37,486 --> 00:00:40,196
供应链、机器人技术等领域的算法。
supply chains, robotics, and more.

8
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:46,532
他就在我们喝一杯咖啡的时间里，彻底改变了世界。
He literally changed the world in the time it takes us to drink a cup of coffee.

9
00:00:47,118 --> 00:00:48,196
你能想象吗？
Can you imagine that?

10
00:00:49,038 --> 00:00:53,956
Edsger Dijkstra 出生于1930年，在荷兰的鹿特丹。
Edgar Dijkstra was born in 1930 in Rotterdam, in the Netherlands.

11
00:00:54,510 --> 00:00:59,588
他在荷兰莱顿的莱顿大学学习数学和物理。
He studied mathematics and physics at Leiden University in Leiden, Netherlands.

12
00:01:00,238 --> 00:01:05,507
让我们来看看他的算法，以及他如何描述那天发生的事情。
Let's take a look at his algorithm and how he described what happened that day.

13
00:01:06,254 --> 00:01:13,028
1956年，Dijkstra 在阿姆斯特丹的数学中心担任程序员。
In 1956, Dijkstra was working as a programmer at the Mathematical Center in Amsterdam.

14
00:01:13,454 --> 00:01:20,900
当时该中心即将推出一台开创性的荷兰计算机，也就是全新的 RMAC 电脑。
The center was about to unveil a pioneering Dutch computer, the new RMAC computer.

15
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:29,572
他想通过选择一个足够有挑战性、能让人们感到惊喜的问题来展示这台电脑的威力，
He wanted to showcase the power of this computer by choosing a problem that would be challenging enough to surprise people,

16
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:36,964
但这个问题又要足够通用，让那些不是计算机专业的人也能理解，甚至觉得有趣。
but general enough so that people who were not specialized in computing could still understand it and even find it interesting.

17
00:01:37,742 --> 00:01:42,052
他选择了寻找两个地点之间最短路径的问题。
He chose the problem of finding the shortest path between two locations.

18
00:01:42,734 --> 00:01:49,572
他问：电脑如何找到从A点到B点最有效的方法？
He asked, How can a computer find the most efficient way to get from point A to point B?

19
00:01:50,286 --> 00:01:54,212
他在工作期间和下班后一直在思考这个问题。
He kept thinking about this during and after his work hours.

20
00:01:54,798 --> 00:01:59,204
令人惊讶的是，灵感在最意想不到的时刻出现了。
Surprisingly, inspiration came during the most unexpected moment.

21
00:01:59,790 --> 00:02:09,668
那天，当 Dijkstra 和他的女朋友逛累了时，他们坐在咖啡馆的露台上喝了一杯咖啡。
When Dijkstra and his girlfriend felt tired from walking around the shops that day, they sat down at a cafe terrace to drink a cup of coffee.

22
00:02:10,126 --> 00:02:12,612
他一直在思考，就在不停地思考。
He kept thinking, he just kept thinking.

23
00:02:13,038 --> 00:02:19,972
他如何找到从荷兰的两个城市——鹿特丹到格罗宁根的最短路径？
How could he find the shortest way to travel from Rotterdam to Groningen, the two cities in the Netherlands?

24
00:02:20,878 --> 00:02:29,732
他最初从这个非常具体的问题开始，但随后他意识到让问题更通用具有巨大的潜力。
He started with that very specific question, but then he realized the potential of making the question more general.

25
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:40,036
与其只考虑两个城市，为什么不给出一个通用的解决方案，来寻找任意两个给定城市之间的最短路径呢？
Instead of only considering two cities, why not come up with a general solution that would find the shortest path between any two given cities?

26
00:02:40,846 --> 00:02:46,880
令人惊讶的是，用他自己的话说，这个解法是经过20分钟的构思才发明的。
Surprisingly, in his own words, the solution was a 20-minute invention.

27
00:02:47,214 --> 00:02:48,836
只要20分钟，仅需20分钟。
20 minutes, that's all it took.

28
00:02:49,550 --> 00:02:57,412
就在他喝完咖啡时，我们现在所熟知的 Dijkstra 算法的基本逻辑已经成型。
By the time he had finished his coffee, the fundamental logic of what we now know as Dijkstras' algorithm was complete.

29
00:02:58,158 --> 00:03:06,788
而且这个算法不仅是正确的，还为我们今天使用的许多现代系统奠定了基础。
And the algorithm was not only correct, but also provided the foundation for many of the modern systems that we use nowadays.

30
00:03:07,566 --> 00:03:13,412
该算法在三年后的1959年正式发表。
The algorithm itself was formally published three years later in 1959.

31
00:03:13,742 --> 00:03:17,360
你现在仍然可以在网上读到最初发表的论文。
You can still read the original publication yourself, online.

32
00:03:17,870 --> 00:03:21,924
它的名字叫《关于与图相关的两个问题的一点说明》。
It's called A Note on Two Problems in Connection with Graphs.

33
00:03:22,926 --> 00:03:28,228
要理解 Dijkstra 的贡献，你需要了解它的基本原理。
To appreciate what Dijkstra came up with, you need to understand its underlying principles.

34
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:30,244
那我们现在就开始深入探讨。
So let's dive in.

35
00:03:31,022 --> 00:03:33,028
首先，什么是算法？
First of all, what is an algorithm?

36
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:45,124
算法是解决问题或达到目标时，需要遵循的一系列非常具体、明确的步骤指令。
An algorithm is a sequence of very, very specific and unambiguous step-by-step instructions that you follow to solve a problem or reach a solution.

37
00:03:45,742 --> 00:03:56,960
软件开发人员使用编程语言来实现这些算法，让计算机按照它们能理解的语言一步步执行这些指令。
Software developers use programming languages to implement these algorithms, making computers follow those instructions step by step in a language they understand.

38
00:03:57,486 --> 00:04:07,300
为了找到任意两个城市之间的最短路径，Dijkstra 必须以更抽象的方式去思考城市之间的可能路径，
To find the shortest path between any two given cities, Dijkstra had to think about the possible paths between the cities in a more abstract way,

39
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:12,068
来表示它们与路径上任何其他城市之间的连接。
representing the connections between them and any other cities in the path.

40
00:04:12,814 --> 00:04:19,844
他通过将现实世界中的道路和城市转化为一种被称为「图」的数据结构来实现这一点。
He did this by translating the physical world of roads and cities into a data structure called graph.

41
00:04:20,589 --> 00:04:27,716
在计算机科学中，你可以把“图”理解为表示事物之间关系或连接的一种方式。
You can think of a graph as a way to represent relationships or connections between things in computer science.

42
00:04:28,686 --> 00:04:32,964
图有两个主要组成部分：节点和边。
Graphs have two main components, nodes and edges.

43
00:04:33,678 --> 00:04:37,028
你可以把节点看作是那些相互连接的事物。
You can think of the nodes as the things that are connected.

44
00:04:37,550 --> 00:04:41,220
在 Dijkstra 算法中，节点代表城市。
In Dijkstra's algorithm, nodes represent cities.

45
00:04:42,158 --> 00:04:50,948
通过将世界视为一系列节点和边的组合，Dijkstra 算法可以应用于几乎任何领域，而不只是道路和城市。
By viewing the world as a series of nodes and edges, Dijkstra's algorithm can be applied to almost anything, not just roads and cities.

46
00:04:51,502 --> 00:05:00,516
在不同的场景下，它们可以代表不同的事物：社交媒体平台上的用户、供应链中的仓库、计算机网络中的路由器，
They could represent different things in different contexts: users in social media platforms, warehouses in supply chains, routers in computer networks,

47
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,876
还有电子游戏中的地图方格，等等。
tiles in video games, and much more.

48
00:05:04,398 --> 00:05:10,116
这里的关键点是，节点代表那些以某种方式相连的事物。
The key takeaway here is that nodes represent things that are somehow connected.

49
00:05:11,054 --> 00:05:13,764
这些连接就是图的边。
These connections are the edges of the graph.

50
00:05:14,382 --> 00:05:20,036
但仅仅知道城市是连接在一起的，还不足以解决 Dijkstra 的问题。
But just knowing that the cities are connected is not enough to solve Dykstra's problem.

51
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:21,956
你还需要更多信息。
You need more information than that.

52
00:05:22,542 --> 00:05:27,204
记住，他当时是在试图寻找两个城市之间的最短路径。
Remember that he was trying to find the shortest path between two cities.

53
00:05:28,110 --> 00:05:35,012
为了找到它，也就是最短路径，你需要知道与每个连接或每条边相关的成本。
To find it, to find the shortest path, you need to know the cost associated with each connection or edge.

54
00:05:35,470 --> 00:05:38,212
这被称为边的权重。
This is known as the weight of the edge.

55
00:05:38,958 --> 00:05:46,820
在 Dijkstra 的问题中，权重代表两个城市之间的距离，或者在它们之间行驶所需的时间，
In Dykstra's problem, weights would represent the distance between two cities, or the time it takes to travel between them,

56
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:50,596
也就是一个某种程度上代表这种连接的抽象数值。
an abstract quantity that somehow represents that connection.

57
00:05:51,150 --> 00:05:55,140
然而，边的权重在不同的场景下可能有不同的含义。
However, edge weight can have different meanings in different contexts.

58
00:05:55,854 --> 00:06:07,268
例如，两个用户之间的连接数量，图像中不同区域像素之间的颜色相似度，或者电子游戏中从一个方格移动到另一个方格的成本，
The number of connections between two users, for example, color similarity between pixels in different regions of an image, the cost of moving from one tile to another in a video game,

59
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:08,400
等等还有更多。
and more.

60
00:06:09,038 --> 00:06:16,100
当图的边具有这些权重时，这个图就被分类为“加权图”。
When the edges of a graph have weights like these, the graph is classified as a weighted graph.

61
00:06:16,718 --> 00:06:19,236
Dijkstra 算法适用于这类图。
Dijkstras algorithm works with this type of graph.

62
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:26,212
它利用权重来寻找最短路径，也就是总权重最低的那条路径。
It uses the weights to find the shortest path, the path with the lowest total weight.

63
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:30,596
让我们通过一个实际的例子来看看这个算法是如何运作的。
Let's see the algorithm in action with a practical example.

64
00:06:31,086 --> 00:06:38,340
假设你正从源节点 A 前往目的地节点 D，而这是城市或节点之间的整体连接情况。
Imagine you're traveling from source node A to destination node D, and this is the overall connection of the cities or the nodes.

65
00:06:39,086 --> 00:06:43,684
节点 A 被称为源节点，也就是你开始整个过程的地方。
Node A is known as the source node, where you're starting the process.

66
00:06:44,590 --> 00:06:48,740
算法首先给每个节点分配一个距离值。
The algorithm starts by assigning a distance value to each node.

67
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:59,108
它将源节点到自身的距离设为 0，而将源节点到图中所有其他节点的距离设为无穷大。
It sets the distance from the source node to itself to zero, and the distance from the source node to all other nodes in the graph to infinity.

68
00:06:59,726 --> 00:07:08,932
这里的「无穷大」只是临时使用的，表示算法目前还不知道这些节点的信息，因为还没访问过它们。
Infinity is only used temporarily here to represent that the algorithm doesn't know anything about those nodes yet because it hasn't visited them.

69
00:07:10,158 --> 00:07:11,940
算法还会记录哪些节点已经被访问过。
Visited nodes are also tracked.

70
00:07:12,718 --> 00:07:16,996
然后，算法开始从源节点 A 开始。
Then the algorithm starts by visiting node A, the source node.

71
00:07:17,518 --> 00:07:18,756
这是起点。
This is the starting point.

72
00:07:19,278 --> 00:07:21,508
它会检查未访问的邻居节点。
It checks its unvisited neighbors.

73
00:07:21,934 --> 00:07:35,908
在这种情况下，这些邻居节点包括距离 A 为 2 的 B 节点（你可以从图表中的距离或权重看到），以及距离 A 为 6 的 C 节点。
In this case, these nodes, the neighbors, are node B with a distance of 2 from node A. You can see the distances or weights over here in the diagram, and node C with a distance of 6 from node A.

74
00:07:36,942 --> 00:07:44,452
由于它们的这些新距离比当前记录的距离要小（记住我们最初设定的都是无穷大），所以它们会被更新。
Since their new distances are smaller than their current distances, remember that we assigned infinity initially, they are updated.

75
00:07:45,326 --> 00:07:48,740
它们的上一个节点也会被更新为 A。
Their previous node is also updated to node A.

76
00:07:49,326 --> 00:07:55,044
只有当路径变短、也就是我们找到更好的、更短的路径时，才会更新距离。
We only update the distances if they are shorter, if we find a better path, a shorter path.

77
00:07:55,566 --> 00:08:04,836
记录节点的序列（就像我们在表格中记录的上一个节点一样）有助于我们在找到最终解后重构出最短路径。
Tracking the sequence of nodes, like the previous nodes that we have here in the table, is helpful to recreate the shortest path once we reach the final solution.

78
00:08:05,262 --> 00:08:12,260
最后，在这一步中，当我们检查完所有邻居并更新了它们的距离后，A 就会被标记为已访问。
And finally, in this step, node A is marked as a visited once we checked all the neighbors and updated their distances.

79
00:08:13,262 --> 00:08:18,852
接着，算法会去访问下一个总边权最小的未访问节点。
Then the algorithm visits the next unvisited node with the lowest total edge weight.

80
00:08:19,342 --> 00:08:24,484
在这个图中，那就是 B 节点，因为它到 A 的距离是 2。
In this graph, that would be node B, since its distance from node A is 2.

81
00:08:25,294 --> 00:08:26,468
所以我们来访问 B 节点。
So let's visit node B.

82
00:08:27,342 --> 00:08:29,636
我们需要检查它的未访问邻居。
We need to check its unvisited neighbors.

83
00:08:30,350 --> 00:08:34,467
这个节点的邻居是 A、C 和 D。
The neighbors of this node are node A, node C, and node D.

84
00:08:35,086 --> 00:08:37,347
但 A 已经被访问过了。
But node A was already visited.

85
00:08:38,222 --> 00:08:41,764
所以这一步我们只考虑 C 和 D。
So we only consider nodes C and D in this step.

86
00:08:42,254 --> 00:08:43,491
让我们从 C 开始。
Let's start with node C.

87
00:08:43,918 --> 00:08:52,068
如果我们选择经过 B 的路径，那么从 A 到 C 的距离将是 2 加 9，
If we choose a path that goes through node B, the distance from node A to node C would be 2 plus 9,

88
00:08:52,334 --> 00:08:53,156
也就是 11。
which is 11.

89
00:08:53,934 --> 00:09:03,236
然而，在我们的表格中，记录的通过之前探索过的另一条路径从 A 到 C 的距离是 6。
However, in our table we have a distance of 6 recorded from node A to node C through a different path that we explored previously.

90
00:09:04,174 --> 00:09:12,388
由于经过 B 的路径比我们目前记录的要长，所以我们不更新距离，而是保留当前的值。
Since taking the path through node B would be longer than what we currently have recorded, we don't update the distance, we just keep the current one.

91
00:09:13,134 --> 00:09:15,204
现在我们到节点 D。
Now let's go to node D.

92
00:09:16,046 --> 00:09:23,780
如果我们选择经过节点 B 的路径，从节点 A 到节点 D 的距离就是 2 加 5，
If we choose a path that goes through node B, the distance from node A to node D would be 2 plus 5,

93
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:24,708
也就是 7。
which is 7.

94
00:09:25,518 --> 00:09:28,868
这比我们目前记录的距离要短。
This is less than the distance that we currently have recorded.

95
00:09:29,262 --> 00:09:33,252
目前是无穷大，所以 7 肯定更好。
Currently it is infinity, so 7 is definitely better.

96
00:09:33,902 --> 00:09:37,860
我们更新这个距离，并将前一个节点改为 B。
We update this distance and the previous node to node B.

97
00:09:39,022 --> 00:09:41,828
最后，我们将节点 B 标记为已访问。
Finally, we mark node B as visited.

98
00:09:42,574 --> 00:09:47,460
现在我们需要访问下一个未访问且总边权最小的节点。
Now we need to visit the next unvisited node with the smallest total edge weight.

99
00:09:48,078 --> 00:09:56,068
在这个图中，那就是节点 C，因为它的距离目前是 6，而从 A 到 B 的距离是 7。
In this graph that would be node C, because its distance is currently 6, while the distance to node B from node A is 7.

100
00:09:56,686 --> 00:09:58,020
所以我们去访问节点 C。
So let's visit node C.

101
00:09:58,606 --> 00:10:01,348
我们需要检查节点 C 的未访问邻居。
We need to check the unvisited neighbors of node C.

102
00:10:02,062 --> 00:10:09,508
节点 C 有三个邻居：A、B 和 D，因为你可以看到它与这些节点有连接，也就是有边。
Node C has three neighbors, node A, node B, and node D since you can see that it has connections with those nodes, it has edges.

103
00:10:10,094 --> 00:10:16,836
但是，由于 A 和 B 已经被标记为已访问，我们只需要检查节点 D。
However, nodes A and B are already marked as visited, so we only need to check node D.

104
00:10:17,710 --> 00:10:20,612
从节点 C 到节点 D 的距离是 8。
The distance from node C to node D is eight.

105
00:10:21,230 --> 00:10:29,188
通过节点 C 从 A 到 D 的总距离是 6 加 8，也就是 14。
The total distance from node A to node D, going through node C, would be six plus eight, which is 14.

106
00:10:29,998 --> 00:10:34,500
目前我们记录的从 A 到 D 的距离是 7。
Currently, the distance that we've recorded from node A to node D is seven.

107
00:10:35,022 --> 00:10:39,908
所以我们保留当前的这个。记住，我们一直在寻找更好的路径，也就是更短的路径。
So we just keep the current one. Remember that we're always looking for a better path, a shorter path.

108
00:10:40,110 --> 00:10:42,244
如果不是更短的，我们就不会更新它。
If it's not shorter, then we don't update it.

109
00:10:42,862 --> 00:10:47,780
而且由于那是节点 C 唯一的未访问邻居，我们将其标记为已访问。
And since that's the only unvisited neighbor of node C, we mark it as visited.

110
00:10:48,622 --> 00:10:53,220
最后，我们前往下一个权重最低的未访问节点。
Finally, we go to the next unvisited node with the lowest total weight.

111
00:10:53,710 --> 00:10:58,052
在这种情况下，只有一个未访问的节点，就是节点 D。
In this case, there's only one unvisited node, which is node D.

112
00:10:58,830 --> 00:11:04,868
由于节点 D 的所有邻居都已被检查并访问，我们只需将其标记为已访问。
Since all the neighbors of node D have already been checked and visited, we just mark it as visited.

113
00:11:04,974 --> 00:11:06,852
我们将节点 D 标记为已访问。
We mark node D as visited.

114
00:11:07,694 --> 00:11:12,740
算法停止了，因为所有节点都已访问，过程也完成了。
And the algorithm stops since all nodes have been visited and the process has been completed.

